    "Picking the right package for a Quatre Bornes wedding usually comes down to three numbers: how many people need a safa, how much time is available before the ceremony, and how detailed the groom's own styling needs to be. A groom-only booking is the simplest option and works well for smaller functions or when family members already have their own arrangements. A groom-plus-family package adds a coordinated look for parents and siblings without the scale of a full baraati booking. The complete package — groom, family and baraat — is the most common choice for larger Quatre Bornes weddings, since it keeps the whole wedding party visually consistent in photographs and keeps the tying schedule managed by one team rather than several. Fabric quality is a separate decision from group size: some families choose a premium fabric for the groom and a simpler, more economical option for the wider baraat, which keeps costs sensible without compromising the groom's look. Whichever package you're considering, sharing your rough budget alongside the guest count helps us recommend something realistic rather than the largest available option by default. We're happy to talk through two or three package options before you decide.",
